This source package is built from the upstream release asset
0c-ime-<version>.tar.xz (not the "Source code" archive generated by GitHub).
That asset includes assets/data/ with the compiled dictionary and
models/pairing.lock.json; a plain Git checkout does not, so run
"make assets MODELS=0" before testing a build from Git.

Dictionary source
  assets/data is built from the bigram TSVs published in the 0c-ime-data
  repository (bigram-<date> release); those inputs are not in the upstream
  tarball (see data/sources/bigram.lock.json and legal/DFSG-free.md).  Debian
  source completeness may need that component tarball as an additional
  upstream source.

Go modules
  go.mod requires Go 1.26.  The build runs through the upstream Makefile with
  GOPROXY=off, so a clean chroot needs Debian-packaged module sources for
  uax29/v2, godbus/dbus/v5, go-winio and x/sys.  Some Debian packages may not
  provide the /v5 or /v2 import paths; patches or a vendor tree will be
  needed.  This is the main open packaging task.

Settings application
  The 0c-settings Tauri application is not built.  The engine and both desktop
  shells work without it, but the Fcitx5 menu entry, the IBus <setup> command
  and the model-download reminder call "0c-update open-settings" and will fail
  until the application is packaged.

Neural runtime
  python3-numpy and python3-onnxruntime are recommended, but upstream pins
  numpy 2.5.3 and onnxruntime 1.30.0 while Debian currently ships older
  versions.  Verify the worker with the packaged versions, or patch it,
  before advertising neural selection as supported.

Tests
  Upstream tests are skipped by default (module dependencies and assets/data).
  The autopkgtest only checks that the dictionary loads with
  "0c-server -check-data".  Enable override_dh_auto_test once the Go modules
  are pinned.

Neural models
  The models are non-free (MIT weights, but no training source) and are
  packaged separately as 0c-ime-models in the non-free archive.  They install
  to /usr/share/0c/neural/{select,punct} and are detected as bundled models.
  debian/control will gain "Suggests: 0c-ime-models" once that package is in
  the archive.

Before the first upload, add the ITP bug number to debian/changelog and fill
in Vcs-Git/Vcs-Browser after creating the packaging repository.
